# Vaultwarden — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/vaultwarden.sops.json.

# Admin panel
# SINGLE QUOTES ARE REQUIRED (finding #30): compose interpolates env_file, so a
# bare argon2 PHC has $argon2id/$v/$m expanded away and Vaultwarden then falls
# through to a PLAINTEXT compare of the mangled string — /admin rejects
# everything and the only clue is a "plain text ADMIN_TOKEN" notice. Do NOT
# $$-escape instead (that advice is for inline `environment:` blocks).
# Empty = /admin disabled, with a warning. Rotating is safe and cheap.
#   docker run --rm vaultwarden/server:1.37.2 /vaultwarden hash
ADMIN_TOKEN='changeme_argon2id_phc_keep_the_single_quotes'

# SSO
# EMPTY is a complete state — SSO_ENABLED is unset in compose, so Vaultwarden
# uses its own master-password accounts. Turning it on also needs
# SSO_ENABLED=true and SSO_AUTHORITY=https://auth.idanreed.com/application/o/vaultwarden.
# The Authentik provider needs exactly ONE redirect URI:
# https://vaultwarden.svc.idanreed.com/identity/connect/oidc-signin — do NOT
# register bitwarden://sso-callback, it never reaches the IdP.
SSO_CLIENT_ID=

# First account is an operator step and deliberately not automated: Bitwarden
# registration is client-side cryptography, and a reimplementation that is
# subtly wrong yields a vault no real client can open. compose ships
# SIGNUPS_ALLOWED=false — log into /admin with ADMIN_TOKEN and invite yourself.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD must NOT live only in this vault: its own backup uses it.
